        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of San Jacinto</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">21 April 1836; the fighting lasted 18 minutes, and the killing of fleeing soldiers went on for hours</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near Lynch's Ferry on Buffalo Bayou, by the San Jacinto River, in present-day La Porte and Deer Park, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Texian Army under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a>, around 800 men (the official count entering battle was 783); the Mexican army under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a>, around 700 men on 20 April and approximately 1,200 to 1,500 after General Martín Perfecto de Cos arrived with 540 reinforcements on the morning of 21 April</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Texians overran the Mexican camp. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Santa Anna</a> and Cos escaped the field but were captured on 22 and 24 April, and Santa Anna later signed the Treaties of Velasco, under which the Mexican army withdrew south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
