    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Houston retreated for weeks before the battle, to the displeasure of his troops, and turned on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Santa Anna</a> only after a captured courier gave him the positions and plans of the Mexican troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</li><li>The Texians numbered around 800 against approximately 1,200 to 1,500 Mexicans, yet the fighting lasted 18 minutes, with 650 Mexican soldiers killed against 11 Texians killed and mortally wounded.</li><li>The force beaten at San Jacinto was not the bulk of the Mexican army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>; about 4,000 more troops under Urrea and Filisola withdrew after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Santa Anna</a> ordered a retreat, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> refused to recognise Texas.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Tejano soldiers in Juan Seguín's company wore playing cards in their hats so that other Texians would not mistake them for Mexican soldiers.</p></aside>
    </section>

